  "details": "Using emote triggers you can make changes to your avatar without holding a gesture.\n\nRight now if you want to apply any of these changes to the Body mesh, you have to split the mesh into two pieces as if you nest the Body in any game objects, the eyetracking breaks.\n\nIf you could set the Body mesh for eyetracking like you do lipsync blendshapes, this will allow you to keep the mesh in one piece while still being able to activate and deactive shapekeys on it freely, leading to more flexibility for avatar creators and a better optimized model.",
